Falsifies `paging::x86_64::verification::the_leaf_keeps_address_and_permissions_apart`.

The defect: `leaf_entry` no longer sets `P`, so every leaf the kernel installs is a
not-present entry. Nothing translates, and on IA-32e a not-present entry's other bits are
ignored by hardware entirely, so the permissions the harness round-trips are decoration on
a page nobody can reach.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(leaf & 1, 1)`, on every input.

**Measured blind before milestone 211.** The harness asserted only
`entry_pa(leaf) == pa` and `leaf_flags(leaf) == flags`. `entry_pa` masks the address bits;
`leaf_flags` reads RW, US, XD, the software kernel-exec bit and G. Neither reads bit 0, so
the present bit could go missing with both round trips intact. Confirmed by applying this
diff against the old phrasing and watching it stay green.

The same rewrite added the address-field assertion, which catches the encoder and its own
decoder moving together; `sv39.verification.the_leaf_keeps_address_and_permissions_apart.patch`
records that half.

diff --git a/crates/paging/src/x86_64.rs b/crates/paging/src/x86_64.rs
index fc3c0dd4..d87a4e96 100644
--- a/crates/paging/src/x86_64.rs
+++ b/crates/paging/src/x86_64.rs
@@ -131,7 +131,7 @@ impl PageFormat for Ia32e {
     }
 
     fn leaf_entry(pa: u64, flags: Flags) -> u64 {
-        (pa & ADDR_MASK) | P | Self::attrs(flags)
+        (pa & ADDR_MASK) | Self::attrs(flags)
     }
 
